Afterlife Server Rules
General Rules:
1.1 Cheats, Exploits & External Tools
• No hacking, cheating, duping, exploiting, or loot cycling.
• No use of Nvidia Inspector or similar tools that give unfair advantages.
• No use of bugged movements such as moonwalking, ice walking, meatballing.
• No vortexing (clipping your head or camera through objects to gain info or advantage).
• Do not abuse any bugs or glitches.
• Game-breaking bugs must be reported via ticket.
• Other bugs should be reported in the designated Discord channel.
• Do not abuse render errors or use them intentionally in PvP or raiding.

1.2 Behavior & Communication
• No hate speech, racism or homophobia.
• No extremely toxic behavior, heavy insults, or targeted harassment.
• Do not call out hackers or accuse people of cheating in global chat – open a ticket instead.
• Do not call out bugs or issues in global chat – use tickets/Discord.

1.3 Meta-Gaming & Accounts
• No meta-gaming:
• Do not leak base locations, PvP spots, or private info from streams/Discord.
• No stream sniping.
• No alt accounts: 1 player = 1 account on the server.
• Players with CF Tools (or similar) access do not share screenshots or information about other players.

1.4 Staff & Admins
• Do not impersonate admins, moderators, or owners.
• Do not publicly accuse staff of abuse – if you suspect abuse, contact the owners via ticket.
• Staff decisions must be respected. Constructive criticism is allowed, but not disrespect.

1.5 Logout
• No logging out in the bunker or key/keycard rooms.
• If the game crashes or the server restarts, you must log back in as soon as possible.
• If you do not log back in, it may be treated as intentional logout.
• No logging out inside enemy bases during or right after a raid. If you disconnect, you must respawn reasonably soon, otherwise it can be counted as combat logging.

1.6 Trader & Special Systems
• Do not abuse the dogtag trader (for example killing your friends just to farm dogtags).
• Do not abuse trader bugs or failures. They must be reported via ticket.


Group Rules:
2.1 Group Size & Alliances
• Maximum group/clan size is 6 players.
• A group do not have more than 6 members online at the same time.
• Alliances are allowed but:
• Alliances together do not exceed 6 players actively playing together in a fight.
• You do not merge alliances into one group to bypass the 6-player limit.

2.2 Group Switching
• Players are not allowed to constantly hop between groups to bypass rules.

2.3 Base Sharing
• Groups and alliances do not share bases.
• Do not store loot or vehicles in a base that does not belong to your own group.
• Alliance bases must be at least 2 km apart.

2.4 Group Limits (Territory, Safes, Vehicles)
• Maximum 2 territories per group
• 1 main base
• 1 second/temporary base
• Maximum 7 big safes per group
• Big safes count towards the codelocked storage limit.
• Maximum 15 codelocked storage per group
• Any type of codelocked storage counts.
• Maximum 8 vehicles of any type per group.

Building Rules:
3.1 Base Location
• No base building directly on main roads.
• Building over a road is allowed if a truck can pass underneath.
• No sky bases or floating bases.
• Your base must follow basic physical logic (one floor may slightly stick out, but no crazy floating structures).
• If you build in or on an existing building, you may only build in/on one building.
• Players do not intentionally block access to wells, wood piles, or other important resources with base parts.

3.2 Number & Size of Bases
• Each group is allowed 2 bases:
• 1 main base
• 1 second/temporary base
• Main base:
• Maximum 15 doors/gates/hatches with codelocks.
• You may build up to 4 walls high from the ground and up to 2 walls high on existing structures.
• Second base:
• Maximum 2 doors/gates/hatches.
• Maximum 2 walls high.
• Must not exceed more than 6 foundations/floors/roofs in total.
• Must be at least 500 m away from your main base.

3.3 Raidability & Fairness
• Your base must be raidable at all times.
• Do not block doors/gates/hatches, including with storage.
• No stacking or glitching storage (no container-in-container or tent-in-tent stacking).
• You do not build in a way that forces raiders to be permanently crawling, crouching, climbing, or jumping through your whole base.
• DayZ ladders may be used in your base, but according to the animation rule they do not be defended while attackers are stuck in the climbing animation.
• Peeks are allowed, but raiders must have a fair chance to defend themselves.
• No “toe peeks” or similar unfair angles.

If an admin classifies a base as unraidable, they may interrupt the raid and adjust the base.
If you are unsure whether your building style is allowed, open a ticket.

Raiding Rules:
4.1 Recording Requirement
• You must record your raid – not just the moment you get into the base.
• Save your clips locally for at least 5 days.
• Staff can ask for the footage at any time.
• Clips are only used by staff and will not be shared with other players.

4.2 Griefing & Loot Handling
• No useless griefing:
• Do not throw massive amounts of loot on the ground just to let it despawn.
• Do not destroy loot for no reason.
• Exception: starter gear or very low-tier items may be dumped.
• Raiders and defenders do not delete loot on purpose (burning, shooting, or other ways of destroying it).

4.3 Glitches & Takeovers
• No glitching into bases that are otherwise impossible to enter (e.g., animation bugs).
• No “takeover bases”:
• If you see a raided or half-built base and want to claim it, open a ticket first.
• No logging out inside enemy bases during or after a raid. If you crash, reconnect and respawn – otherwise it counts as logging out.

4.4 Base Elements During Raids
• Do not remove resources from territory station – this counts as griefing.
• Do not dismantle base elements just to collect materials and kits.
• Only dismantle what is necessary to get in or out.
• You may only raid from the soft side (inner side) of walls, except when fixing building errors or bypassing doors in a reasonable way.
• Over-dismantling can be interpreted as griefing.

4.5 Movement & Boosting
• You are allowed to crawl through windows.
• You are allowed to boost with:
• 2 players, 1 item, or 1 land vehicle.
• You do not boost using helicopters (e.g., jumping onto a hovering heli to boost into bases).
• Helicopter raids are allowed:
• Landing on/in bases.
• Jumping from the heli seat onto balconies or base structures.

4.6 Animation Rule (Defenders)
• If your base has ladders or other elements that force attackers to play an animation (climb, vault, etc.),
• You do not use that animation state to gain an advantage.
• You do not defend positions that require the attacker to be stuck in an animation.
• Video evidence is required in such cases.

Additional:
• Combat logging in PvP situations (logging out shortly after being shot at or spotted) may be punished as a rulebreak.

Ban Policy:
Ban Policy

• For most rules, we use a strike system.
• Examples: combat logging, minor bug abuse (depending on severity).
• Certain severe rulebreaks result in an immediate permanent ban.
• Examples: cheating, hacking, extreme racism, heavy abuse or exploitation.

We have zero tolerance against:
• Cheats and hacks
• Massive abuse of bugs
• Racism, hate speech, or homophobia
Rules may be changed at any time without prior notice.
It is your responsibility to stay up to date with the rules.

Staff & Ticket

• Staff decisions are to be respected and accepted.
• You may give feedback or criticism, but it must be constructive and not disrespectful.
• Staff work in their free time – this is not a job. Please be patient.
• It may take up to 12 hours for a ticket to receive a response.

Video Evidence & Compensation:
Video Evidence Tips

• We recommend using tools like Medal.tv or NVIDIA Shadowplay – they have minimal performance impact.
• We do not recommend OBS for constant recording due to its performance cost.
• Good video evidence makes support cases easier and increases the chance of refunds in valid situations.

Compensation

• We do not compensate for typical DayZ bugs or normal gameplay issues.
• Compensation is only given for:
• Server crashes
• Clear server-side errors
• Verified staff/system mistakes with sufficient evidence
